From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 22:35:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: dt-bindings: ti,tas27xx: Add apple,deferred-shutdown

On an AOP-fed speaker stream the TDM bus keeps running for a while after
the playback stream stops, and the amplifiers' current and voltage sense
slots are still sampled in that time. An amplifier put in software
shutdown then can leave garbage in its sense slots.

Add a property for such amplifiers: they must not enter software
shutdown until the bus has stopped.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
(cherry picked from commit b9949a8dfb99de3fe56b2366af8d020f7caba762)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/ti,tas27xx.yaml | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/ti,tas27xx.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/ti,tas27xx.yaml
index 99eebcfabb..05c2ab00c4 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/ti,tas27xx.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/ti,tas27xx.yaml
@@ -66,6 +66,15 @@ properties:
       down, and no member enables it again until the driver is reloaded.
       A member needs its fault interrupt.
 
+  apple,deferred-shutdown:
+    type: boolean
+    description:
+      The amplifier's TDM bus keeps running for a while after its playback
+      stream stops, as on an AOP-fed speaker stream, and its current and
+      voltage sense slots are still sampled in that time. The amplifier
+      must not enter software shutdown until the bus has stopped. One shut
+      down while the bus still runs can leave garbage in its sense slots.
+
   ti,imon-slot-no:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
     description: TDM TX current sense time slot.
